#: ../../architecture.md:1
msgid "How it works"
msgstr "Cómo funciona"

#: ../../architecture.md:3
msgid ""
"**Claiming**: `UPDATE ... WHERE id = (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED "
"LIMIT 1) RETURNING ...` — safe for multiple worker processes running in "
"parallel."
msgstr ""
"**Claiming**: `UPDATE ... WHERE id = (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED "
"LIMIT 1) RETURNING ...` — seguro para múltiples procesos worker corriendo "
"en paralelo."

#: ../../architecture.md:4
msgid ""
"**Wakeup**: a Postgres trigger emits `NOTIFY task_psql_new` on every "
"`INSERT` of a `READY` task (fired after commit, so tasks created inside a"
" transaction only wake the worker once it commits). The worker blocks on "
"`LISTEN` with a heartbeat fallback (`TASK_WORKER_HEARTBEAT_S`) to catch "
"deferred tasks whose `run_after` has elapsed without a fresh `NOTIFY`."
msgstr ""
"**Activación**: un trigger de Postgres emite `NOTIFY task_psql_new` en "
"cada `INSERT` de una tarea `READY` (disparado después del commit, así que "
"las tareas creadas dentro de una transacción solo despiertan al worker "
"una vez que esa transacción hace commit). El worker bloquea en `LISTEN` "
"con un fallback por heartbeat (`TASK_WORKER_HEARTBEAT_S`) para cubrir "
"tareas diferidas cuyo `run_after` venció sin un `NOTIFY` nuevo."

#: ../../architecture.md:5
msgid ""
"**Concurrency**: the worker's main thread claims one task at a time and "
"submits it to a `ThreadPoolExecutor`; a `Semaphore` limits how many are "
"in flight before claiming the next. Each thread closes its own database "
"connection when it's done with a task — with Django's native connection "
"pool enabled, that returns the connection to the pool instead of dropping"
" the socket, which avoids a connection leak that recurring background "
"threads are prone to."
msgstr ""
"**Concurrencia**: el thread principal del worker claimea una tarea a la "
"vez y la somete a un `ThreadPoolExecutor`; un `Semaphore` limita cuántas "
"hay en vuelo antes de claimear la siguiente. Cada thread cierra su propia "
"conexión a la base al terminar una tarea — con el connection pool nativo "
"de Django activo, eso devuelve la conexión al pool en vez de cortar el "
"socket, evitando una fuga de conexiones a la que son propensos los "
"threads de background que se reutilizan."

#: ../../architecture.md:6
msgid ""
"**Retries**: on failure, a task is rescheduled with `run_after = now() + "
"backoff_base * 2^(attempt - 1)`, until `max_attempts` is reached, at "
"which point it's marked `FAILED`."
msgstr ""
"**Reintentos**: ante una falla, la tarea se reprograma con `run_after = "
"now() + backoff_base * 2^(attempt - 1)`, hasta alcanzar `max_attempts`, "
"momento en el que se marca `FAILED`."
